body:
The destination insert and source delete are separate manifest rewrites, so they do not form one rename transaction. Two concurrent renames of the same source can both publish destinations; one call then errors during physical cleanup after its destination is already visible. A failed call has therefore mutated durable namespace state. Use one conflict-aware rename mutation that validates the source, destination, and destination namespace and replaces the row in a single `rewrite_manifest`; make physical cleanup best-effort after that commit.

